      "description": "Playwrights know you never get a second chance to make a first impression. Directors cast actors who have mastered the art of the dramatic entrance. Typographers pick fonts that spearhead a design with the right voice. Such as Kaybe Serif: a transitional typeface for a memorable first impression in large and medium sizes. With sense and sensibility, it’s at its strongest whenever smartness, emotion, sophistication, luxury, and culture come into play—where tradition meets progress. Its hallmark: true italic styles with an array of swash capitals and discretionary ligatures. “All the world’s a page, and all the fonts and pictures merely players”: Leave a mark on this page with Kaybe Serif.",
